SPEC = {'file': 'cover_penta_applied_ai_ml_engineer', 'label': 'Penta Applied AI / ML Engineer', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Applied AI / ML Engineer position at Penta in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is unusually close to what I have actually done: building LLM-based tools with retrieval, and evaluating their outputs carefully before anyone relies on them.', 'What attracts me most to Penta is that the AI work is practical and close to the people using it, and that the role expects engineers to build quickly with tools such as Claude Code and then check whether the output is good enough. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality. This taught me that how you evaluate an AI system matters as much as how you build it.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'On the machine learning side, my MSc work spans predictive modelling, NLP and evaluation. My dissertation builds predictive and causal models on 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application so that people can run scenarios without touching the code. I also led a group project building a clinical NLP pipeline that parsed free-text radiology reports into structured features using fine-tuned transformer models, and evaluated where vision-language models failed against the text-derived signals. Explaining results clearly to people who do not want the method is something I have done at Ipsos Strategy3 and with pharmaceutical client stakeholders.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience with LLM pipelines, retrieval and evaluation could contribute to Penta's applied AI work. I am based in London. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship."]}
